   "notes": [
    "Actual results for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2024, as the city reported them to the Census Bureau's Annual Survey of State and Local Government Finances. Not a budget.",
    "Public schools are run by parish school boards, which are separate governments, so they are not included. Residents also pay Terrebonne Parish.",
    "Covers every fund, including water, sewer, electric and other utilities. Debt service counts interest and principal repaid; borrowing and transfers between funds are left out.",
    "Payments to other governments ($2,740,000) are left out, because the government receiving them reports that spending.",
    "Courts, legal services, public buildings, housing and community development count as overhead.",
    "Debt is long-term debt outstanding plus short-term debt at year end.",
    "Political money is not scored: no candidates for mayor, council or board of aldermen and chief of police of City of Houma e-filed contributions with the Board of Ethics since 2023.",
    "Transparency practices have not been checked yet, so they are not scored.",
    "Cameras: 7 license-plate cameras are mapped inside City of Houma's borders in OpenStreetMap (6 made by Flock Safety), not counting cameras tagged as run by stores, malls, schools or state and regional agencies. Flock cameras count as a red flag whoever runs them. Other brands count only when the government is the recorded operator, since many have no operator recorded.",
    "Red flags: surveillance programs come from the EFF Atlas of Surveillance, a public database of news reports and public records, searched on 2026-10-18. A town or county with none listed may still have programs nobody has reported. Data center deals and corporate tax breaks have not been checked for Louisiana yet. Most records carry no dollar amount, so each documented program costs a quarter of the red-flag points instead of being counted as spending."
   ],
